module

public import Rule30Open.Columns.ReachRefuted
public import Rule30Open.Columns.NineTraps

/-!
# Entry into 41 more carried traps is false, refuted by the same wall carried farther into its background

A wall of the trap modules, carried leftward by its chain, reaches a background periodic in time and space after `start`
columns: from there on column `D + q` is column `D`. When `start > 0` (the walls of periods 9, 11, 12 and 13 here), the
background's own half beside a column that repeats a block is in the block's carried trap at none of its labels; the
same holds beside the columns of one block of period 14, whose wall has `start = 0`, that the background's symmetries do
not map to the block's own. The trap carried to a distance `D = x + i q`, where column `x` of the background repeats the block
and `D - start` is at least the width of the block's trap, is then a trap of the same block whose states, cut to that
width, are that background half: apart from the trap. A right half started in it never enters, so entry into the trap is
false.

* `sib_<trap>`: the sibling, with `sib_<trap>_closed`.
* `sib_<trap>_cut`: the trap's states as a set of windows of [ReachRefuted](ReachRefuted.md), with `_holds` and
  `_avoids`.
* `<trap>_not_absorption_sibling`: the refutation, by `not_absorption_fwd`.

The tables come from `python -m computations.background_prefix --lean-siblings`. The natural-language argument is
`BackgroundSiblings.md`, beside this file.
-/

@[expose] public section

-- Sequential elaboration: the kernel checks would otherwise run in parallel and stack their memory.
set_option Elab.async false

namespace Rule30Open

open Ruliology.CellularAutomata BitGame

